Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sunxi: number IRQ banks from the first populated bank

The first populated bank need not be PA. Start the last-bank and IRQ
bank counters before their first valid index so PB starts at IRQ bank 0.
This also handles leading populated banks that have no IRQ support.

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi-dt.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi-dt.c
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi-dt.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi-dt.c
@@ -208,8 +208,8 @@
 	 * Assign the function's memory and fill in GPIOs, IRQ and a sentinel.
 	 * The extra functions will be filled in later.
 	 */
-	irq_bank = 0;
-	last_bank = 0;
+	irq_bank = -1;
+	last_bank = -1;
 	for (i = 0; i < npins; i++) {
 		struct sunxi_desc_pin *pin = &pins[i];
 		int bank = (pin->pin.number - pin_base) / PINS_PER_BANK;
